<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      WP-T: the launch window background matches the default palette's light canvas
      (#F2F1ED = FmPalettes.of(PaletteId.Forest, dark = false).canvas, 配色方案 §6.1 暖灰墨绿) so the first frame
      does not flash white while Compose starts. values-night\themes.xml overrides
      the same name with the dark tokens (#181C19 = FmPalettes.of(PaletteId.Forest, dark = true).canvas) and a dark
      Material base so the status-bar icons start out light.

      WP-X3 §3 (WP-F2 D2): the pair above follows the **system** night mode, but the
      in-app 外观 setting can be 深色 while the system is 浅色. In that case the
      launch window was the light one and the user saw a 700–800 ms white flash
      before the first dark Compose frame. MainActivity now reads the stored
      appearance in onCreate *before* `super.onCreate` and calls `setTheme` with one
      of the two explicit styles below, so the launch window always matches the
      resolved appearance. They are declared in values/ (no -night variant) on
      purpose: an explicit `setTheme` must not be re-resolved against the system
      night mode.

      配色方案 §6：这两支样式只能编码默认配色的画布。四套配色各自的画布见
      `Palette.kt`；MainActivity 读到用户选的配色后会用 `window.setBackgroundDrawable`
      覆盖这里的底色，所以非默认配色也不会闪一帧暖灰。
    -->
    <style name="Theme.FrameMark" parent="@android:style/Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">#F2F1ED</item>
    </style>

    <!-- Light appearance, forced regardless of the system night mode. -->
    <style name="Theme.FrameMark.Light" parent="@android:style/Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">#F2F1ED</item>
    </style>

    <!-- Dark appearance, forced regardless of the system night mode. -->
    <style name="Theme.FrameMark.Dark" parent="@android:style/Theme.Material.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">#181C19</item>
    </style>
</resources>
